    "body": "> I'm not entirely sure of the motivation for originally proposing this\r\n\r\nThe `slot:dir()` rules are there to implement the behavior that the directionality of a slot element is taken from the shadow root, not from the slot's parent. See https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3699#issuecomment-951423468 This is in order to preserve (by default) the flow of directionality through the light DOM, which would otherwise be interrupted by directionality settings in the shadow DOM.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
